#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Python API for the latest version of Qiskit Fermions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Python API"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Python API {#install-the-python-api}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prerequisites {#prerequisites}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, create a minimal environment with only Python installed in it. Use "
"[Python virtual "
"environments](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/venv.html).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Activate your new environment.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are two primary ways to install this package: from PyPI or from "
"source. The preferred method is to install from PyPI:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install from PyPI {#install-from-pypi}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install from source {#install-from-source}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you plan to develop in the repository you should install from source.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, Qiskit must be installed in the same Python environment that you "
"install `qiskit-fermions` in. The simplest way to do this is from PyPI, but "
"you can install Qiskit from source if you want to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next, clone the `qiskit-fermions` repository.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, install the Rust toolchain, upgrade pip, and enter the repository. "
"Refer to the [Rust documentation](https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install) "
"for instructions on installing the toolchain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install the remaining `build` dependencies. If you plan on developing in the"
" repository, install the `dev` dependencies.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The next step is to install `qiskit-fermions` to the virtual environment.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Hint\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  You can also perform an editable install while still compiling the "
"underlying Rust crate in `release` mode:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Some features rely on optional dependencies. To install all of them, use "
"the `all` extra:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Refer to the `[project.optional-dependencies]` section of "
"[pyproject.toml](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-"
"fermions/blob/main/pyproject.toml) to see which dependency groups are "
"available.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can optionally verify that the installation was successful. The simplest"
" test is to try and import one of the classes provided by the `qiskit-"
"fermions` package, as in the following example:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "If this completes successfully, your installation worked.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  You can also run the entire Python test suite:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  To additionally run the tests that exercise optional dependencies, install"
" the extras and use the `testoptional` target:\n"
msgstr ""
